   "notes": "Own exact-integer computations from the definition found 0 violations: m<=128, n<=8000 and m 129..520, n<=1000. Equality never occurs for any m = 15 mod 16 (up to 511), and every claimed equality set holds. A line-by-line check of F1-F4, Lemma R, Lemma W, the readout, the even-case invariant, the odd-case T' rules, crude bound (2), the closed form of r_{0,0}, and an independent binomial-basis certificate (own degree bound 4F+6) found no gaps. Write-up repairs: state that T maps Z[y] to Z[y]; the degree-bound comment (4F+4 vs 4F+5) is inconsistent; line 150 asserts >=11 where the certificate only checks >=8 (8 suffices)."
  },
